    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The schema graph is a graph, and it is published",
      "prov:value": "`directoryForGraph` throws when several directories declare a graph — the\n`wggr` guard, which exists because returning the first silently once resolved\n`cat-harness` to `schemas/` and wrote 37 sidecars against the wrong subjects on\na run that exited 0."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The three answers that are not \"fine\", and what each one means",
      "prov:value": "**The fix for noise is never a deny-list.** The first version of the reader\ncollected every identifier and reported `z` as the graph's most-referenced\nmissing declaration, 175 times."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`@ref` — declaring the edge the reader cannot find",
      "prov:value": "Two equally-near targets is an *ambiguous tag*,\nnot a winner: picking the first is the `wggr` failure one level down, an answer\nthat looks resolved and may be the wrong schema."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The control worked in both directions",
      "prov:value": "The same run found the hand-drawn diagram wrong: it draws\n`SkillDefinition *-- SkillSchemaRef : schemas`, and `SkillDefinitionSchema`\nhas no `schemas` field at all. That corroborates bean `3lbz`, which found\n`SkillDefinition.schemas` had no readers and its only referencing code was a\nscript nothing invokes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3lbz"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Adding or changing a schema — the loop",
      "prov:value": "`schema:viz:check` is worth running locally and is deliberately **not** a CI\ngate (owner, 2026-09-20). The projection derives from the WHOLE repository, so\non a fast-moving repo the check reddens when somebody else merges rather than\nwhen you forget — which is not an omission, and not what a gate is for.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Keeping the projection's gate honest",
      "prov:value": "The projection is committed. It HAD a staleness gate, and the gate came out —\nbecause **a staleness gate is only worth having if its red means an\nomission**, and this one's did not."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Keeping the projection's gate honest",
      "prov:value": "The same reasoning removed the per-module declaration list: a declaration\nalready names its module, so the list was one fact written twice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where a viewer publishes — TWO rules, not three",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-20:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Rule 1 is the canonical address; a bare `<base>/<visualizer>/` is an opt-in alias",
      "prov:value": "The owner, 2026-10-07 (bean `t4xb`): *\"`<base_url>/<visualizer>` is an opt-in\n(for prettiness or so), but `<base_url>/<harness>/<visualizer>` always\nworks.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean t4xb",
        "2026-10-07"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Rule 1 is the canonical address; a bare `<base>/<visualizer>/` is an opt-in alias",
      "prov:value": "**Built 2026-10-09** (owner: *\"Need harness to declare visualizer is\nrenderedBy\"*): a visualiser is declared by its harness in `visualisers`, and\nits `alias` is the opt-in.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Rule 1 is the canonical address; a bare `<base>/<visualizer>/` is an opt-in alias",
      "prov:value": "Link to the canonical form;\nan alias is for a person typing a URL. The disk side of bean `t4xb` — a remote\nmount landing at `<name>/` — is still open, in [`remote-mount`](remote-mount.md).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean t4xb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "When the two collide — the handler wins",
      "prov:value": "An instance that is **both** — this one renders every graph here AND has a site\nof its own — makes rules 1 and 2 name the same path, `<base>/<instance>/`, and\nnothing above chooses between them. The owner settled it on 2026-09-21:\n\n> harness handler wins.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "When the two collide — the handler wins",
      "prov:value": "The authored page\nthat sat there moved to `docs/platform.md`, and `gen-handler-index.ts` generates\nthe route's index from `harnessTiles`. Bean `8h42`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 8h42"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "When the two collide — the handler wins",
      "prov:value": "This ruling was recorded on the generator and in the bean for four hours and\n**not here, beside the rules it arbitrates** — which is\n[`symbiotic-interaction`](../../conduct/conduct-core/symbiotic-interaction.md) §2's third worked example\nand the reason that section exists."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "When the two collide — the handler wins",
      "prov:value": "That\nis rule 2's namespace, and a viewer parked there squats on the instance's own\nsite. An earlier draft was about to publish the IRIS replica's `library/` exactly there,\non a misreading of \"path to dir handled\" as the page's address rather than as\nwhat the page shows."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`docs/` is the same shape, and its subject means something specific",
      "prov:value": "Owner, same day:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "`docs/` is the same shape, and its subject means something specific",
      "prov:value": "**Measured 2026-09-20 and not yet true:** only `cat-harness` has a `docs/`\ndirectory and only it declares one, with `dependents: \"skip\"` — which was\nprecisely what stopped a dependent from getting its own.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The relationship diagram — what is defined here, and HOW it is linked",
      "prov:value": "A collapsible panel at the top of the viewer draws the declarations the page is\nscoped to as **UML class boxes wired by their edges, each edge labelled with\nthe field it goes through**. That label is the point. Owner, 2026-09-20:\n\n> so you can see Role is linked to Task (how) etc. / the relatioship diagram\n> or so",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "It is scoped, and refusing is an answer",
      "prov:value": "Owner, same day: **\"not the WHOLE thing\"**, and *\"what's defined in that KG\nharness\"*."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "One hop of context, because counting an edge is not showing it",
      "prov:value": "`RoleDefSchema --skills--> SkillDefinitionSchema` spans two files, so\nfiltering to `role-graph.ts` drew Role with its most interesting relation\nmissing and reported the loss as a number."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "One hop of context, because counting an edge is not showing it",
      "prov:value": "**The fade is load-bearing.** It shipped broken once: the CSS landed but the\nclass was never applied, so context boxes were indistinguishable from real\nones — a diagram that quietly widened its own scope."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Layout",
      "prov:value": "Dragging and alternate arrangements are bean `whbf`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean whbf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Clicking a box opens its definition",
      "prov:value": "Which is what makes the diagram navigation rather than a poster — the owner's\noriginal ask was *\"browsable, so i can give overview like browsing\"*."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Orphan pages — a generator that writes must also prune",
      "prov:value": "Measured, bean `ankg`: #604 renamed `folio-assist-sci/` to\nthe science layer.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ankg",
        "#604"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "607), `orphanSubjectPages`, and `prunableDashboards` (`state-visualizer.ts`).",
      "prov:value": "Each is correct; the multiplicity is the defect, tracked as bean `s8nu`. A new\ngenerator imports `orphanSubjectPages` rather than minting a fifth.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean s8nu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-26",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Editing a viewer — no backticks",
      "prov:value": "A backtick **anywhere** inside it — including in a JavaScript comment in the\nembedded script — terminates the string, and the failure surfaces as a parse\nerror a couple of hundred lines from the mistake. It has happened twice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-27",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the boundaries are",
      "prov:value": "- **An unwired generator is worse than none.** Three schema generators were\n  written here before the current one and all three rotted, because nothing\n  ever asked whether their output still matched their input."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/schema-management.md#provenance-28",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`docs/` is the same shape, and its subject means something specific",
      "prov:value": "**Measured 2026-09-20 and not yet true:** only `cat-harness` has a `docs/`\ndirectory and only it declares one, with `dependents: \"skip\"` — which was\nprecisely what stopped a dependent from getting its own. **Superseded\n2026-09-30** (option A): `docs` is a `perInstance` kind, so every instance\ninheriting it gets its own, and each existing `<instance>/docs/` is a member\nof the one declared subgraph. Nothing was declared\nagainst an absent directory here, because a declared-but-absent directory is\nthe `dh4f` defect. Bean `n0nf` carries the same `skip` finding from the root's\nside.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean n0nf"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
